WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.300
FlowBatch: how to use it, from one video to anime clips in Google Flow

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:08.900
Set up: open your Flow project, then click the FlowBatch icon to open the side panel.

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:20.900
Step 1 of 5: Split your video. Load it in Frame extractor, set Clip length to 7 s and press Split video.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:32.900
Step 2 of 5: Send the clips to Flow. Send to Flow uploads all 3 in one batch. Then + Assets lets you @mention them.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:44.900
Step 3 of 5: Write one prompt. Mention @clip_001, then press One prompt per asset: one prompt for every clip.

00:00:45.200 --> 00:01:05.900
Step 4 of 5: Press Start. FlowBatch picks each clip in Flow, types the prompt, submits it and waits for the video.

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:19.800
Step 5 of 5: Your anime clips. Each result downloads by itself, one file per prompt, into your project folder.

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:30.600
Posted as a Reel: the same Flow results, cut together and posted on Instagram. Instagram @bidibambudum · Threads @bidibambudum · instagram.com/reel/DduLARnT2F5. The same 9:16 MP4 fits Instagram Reels, Facebook Reels, Threads, YouTube Shorts and TikTok.

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:37.000
Split, Send to Flow, Prompt, Start, Download. Enjoyed it? Star FlowBatch on GitHub: github.com/Manish-404/Flow_batch · Instagram & Threads: @bidibambudum
